  "lawGrade": "DERIVED",
  "lawGradeScale": "v4 law grading scale (native canon scale, strongest first): DERIVED, LOCKED, MAPPED, PARTIAL, SPLIT, OPEN, DEFINITIONAL. Mapping to C0-C6 unruled - tracked as OI-0011.",
  "statementTechnical": "Second Law of Thermodynamics (Clausius): dS_total/dt >= 0; internal entropy production dS_internal/dt >= 0; dS = dS_internal + dS_boundary. A closed system cannot reduce internally produced disorder without boundary transfer. Canonical grade DERIVED - the strongest law: the physics structure already contains the spiritual claim ('nothing was added'). Entropy production maps to judgment/consequence; a closed moral system cannot repair its own damage; the boundary term maps to atonement - grace received from outside the system. Recorded kill test: pure ascent on a product coherence landscape does not automatically generate decay; if decay appears only after arbitrary tuning, Level 2 fails leg 2 of the proof standard (LOCK GATE: dX/dt must reproduce Law 5 decay structurally).",
  "statementPlain": "Disorder accumulates by default and a closed system cannot clean itself up - repair has to cross the boundary from outside. Canon grades this the strongest law because nothing was inserted: the second law already says what the theology says about judgment and atonement. Even here, honesty is load-bearing: the boundary-transfer structure is formalized (receipt external to this repo), but identifying the boundary term with atonement remains a theological bridge claim, not proven, and one verification gate is still open - the framework's own dynamics must reproduce decay without tuning.",
  "mathematicalForm": "dS_total/dt >= 0; dS = dS_internal + dS_boundary; closed system: no internal reduction of produced disorder without boundary transfer",
  "mathFormNormal": "dS_total/dt >= 0; dS = dS_internal + dS_boundary; closed system: no internal reduction of produced disorder without boundary transfer",
